<title>UK: Officials confirm EU free market grain awards.</title>
<headline>Officials confirm EU free market grain awards.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following licences to export free market grain to non-EU countries, member-country officials confirmed.</p>
<p>		  Tonnage	  Maximum rebate</p>
<p>Barley	   89,200	  15.90  Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>Rye		 4,000	  29.98  Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>Oats		6,000	  21.94  Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>(From Sweden and Finland for countries other than Switzerland and Liechtenstein)</p>
<p>Oats		2,500	  21.75  Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>(From Sweden and Finland for Switzerland and Liechtenstein)</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
